import Googology.Trans.BMS.TrioRules3
import Googology.Trans.BMS.TrioRules2Sheet

/-!
# Fix E against the sheet

`TrioRules2Sheet.lean` calibrates `TrioRules2.lean` on every row of
[`tools/omega_alpha_rows.tsv`](https://github.com/koteitan/trio/blob/main/tools/omega_alpha_rows.tsv)
with the verdicts of [TRIO-SHEET-41.md](TRIO-SHEET-41.md).  This file checks that
Fix E (`TrioRules3.lean`) keeps all of that:

* on all 817 distinct labels (the 808 distinct labels of the 813 rows, and the 9
  corrected labels of the `L` rows) the new rules give the matrix of `TrioRules2`,
  except on the printed label of row 3552, where they give the new standard matrix;
* **the order check**: the 783 matrices of `TrioRules2Sheet.lean` and the new matrix
  of the printed label of row 3552 (784 matrices, 306,936 pairs) are in the order of
  their labels under `cmpOrd`.

All of it is `#guard`s: a calibration, not a theorem.
-/

